{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383778-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon","id":1383778,"title":"Heroic spirits in Typemoon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-25T08:53:18-07:00","id":1383778,"title":"Heroic spirits in Typemoon?","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> I used to ask the same question in WtA section:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381944-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ts-in-typemoon</a><br /> <br /> The link: <a href=\"https://typemoon.fandom.com/wiki/Heroic_Spirit\" target=\"_blank\">https://typemoon.fandom.com/wiki/Heroic_Spirit</a><br /> <br /> So to be simple, heroic spirits are spirits of heroes who achieved great deeds in life, having become objects of worship after their deaths<br /> <br /> but I was told that they seem to be a sort of thing in Mage, so what\u2019s your idea about this? Had you fanmade any rule about this? Share your ideas!<br /> <br /> *At first I think they are more suitable to a heroic game, which is closer to WtA, battle the evil wymish creatures and save the world, and I think they\u2019re much like the ancestor spirits (Of course someone had corrected this in that post, don\u2019t mention this anyway)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T17:29:48-07:00","id":1383876,"title":"","content":"Well, in Mage, the Umbra is described as a place where all sorts of spirit realms exist, including places where all the various aspects of gods and other beings can be found. There are parts of the Umbra where you can probably find the platonic ideal embodiment of everything that everyone has ever thought of or imagined, various heavens and hells and the homes of different divinities, and even places of incomprehensible absolute abstraction. It wouldn't be absurd to find the Throne of Heroes exactly as portrayed in the Typemoon universe among these worlds and then for a Mage to then somehow figure out how to summon beings from that realm. <br /> <br /> Conceptually, they fit perfectly in Mage. Mechanically, I'm not entirely sure Mage is the best system to portray such beings with. If you built them as Umbrood, you'd probably end up making all sorts of weird custom powers for them that you might as well write &quot;Fate, the Summoning&quot; or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-25-2020, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T18:42:36-07:00","id":1383889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383778-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon?p=1383876#post1383876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conceptually, they fit perfectly in Mage. Mechanically, I'm not entirely sure Mage is the best system to portray such beings with. If you built them as Umbrood, you'd probably end up making all sorts of weird custom powers for them that you might as well write &amp;quot;Fate, the Summoning&amp;quot; or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s why I want to put them in Werewolf originally. <br /> <br /> Making them more accessible, just like Ancestor spirits, and their realm, Throne of Heroes, become something like one of the 13 Realms. Of course I had been told heroic spirits are not ancestor spirits exactly, but they\u2019re much like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T19:49:03-07:00","id":1383898,"title":"","content":"Aren't spirits mechanically similar in Mage and Werewolf? <br /> <br /> If I was to try to stick them in the WOD without too much effort, I'd probably end up using a mix of Sorcerer and Mage and then importing a bunch of stuff from Exalted 1st edition for the Heroic Spirit part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T22:31:51-07:00","id":1383910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383778-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon?p=1383876#post1383876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in Mage, the Umbra is described as a place where all sorts of spirit realms exist, including places where all the various aspects of gods and other beings can be found. There are parts of the Umbra where you can probably find the platonic ideal embodiment of everything that everyone has ever thought of or imagined, various heavens and hells and the homes of different divinities, and even places of incomprehensible absolute abstraction. It wouldn't be absurd to find the Throne of Heroes exactly as portrayed in the Typemoon universe among these worlds and then for a Mage to then somehow figure out how to summon beings from that realm.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, they fit perfectly in Mage. Mechanically, I'm not entirely sure Mage is the best system to portray such beings with. If you built them as Umbrood, you'd probably end up making all sorts of weird custom powers for them that you might as well write &quot;Fate, the Summoning&quot; or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They function as fairly powerful familiars but.. familiars feed them quint and watch them go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}